"""
A module for reading and writing values out of nested JSON-like data using path strings.

Features:
- Reading (get) with nested dicts, lists, and scalars.
- Writing (set) with automatic container creation.
- Deleting (delete) from dicts and lists.
- Wildcard support `[*]` for list/tuple/mapping traversal.

Path syntax:
- Names: one or more characters other than ., [, ], "
- [N]: integer index (supports negative)
- ["..."]: quoted key for special characters
- [*]: wildcard (only valid in set/delete for list/tuple/mapping traversal)
- Empty string: refers to the whole object

Exceptions:
- PathError: Syntax error, type mismatch, missing value, or invalid operation.
